t do not significantly impair daily functioning. They","bbox":[91.0395,167.36551,543.4585,178.36551],"origin":[91.0395,175.86499],"font":"Helvetica","size":11.0,"colour":"#000000","direction":[1.0,0.0]},{"text":"are unlikely to meet the diagnostic criteria for depression or anxiety.","bbox":[91.0395,179.46548,419.95047,190.46548],"origin":[91.0395,187.96497],"font":"Helvetica","size":11.0,"colour":"#000000","direction":[1.0,0.0]},{"text":"- Mild (11–14): Scores in this range indicate mild psychological distress of clinical significance,","bbox":[91.0395,191.56546,548.2984,202.56546],"origin":[91.0395,200.06494],"font":"Helvetica","size":11.0,"colour":"#000000","direction":[1.0,0.0]},{"text":"where symptoms are noticeable but unlikely to disrupt daily functioning. People in this range","bbox":[91.0395,203.66544,537.95856,214.66544],"origin":[91.0395,212.16492],"font":"Helvetica","size":11.0,"colour":"#000000","direction":[1.0,0.0]},{"text":"probably meet the criteria for depression, anxiety, or another mental disorder.","bbox":[91.0395,215.76541,467.03046,226.76541],"origin":[91.0395,224.26489],"font":"Helvetica","size":11.0,"colour":"#000000","direction":[1.0,0.0]},{"text":"- Moderate (15–19): Scores in this range reflect moderate distress, with symptoms that are","bbox":[91.0395,227.86539,531.20459,238.86539],"origin":[91.0395,236.36487],"font":"Helvetica","size":11.0,"colour":"#000000","direction":[1.0,0.0]},{"text":"pronounced and interfere with the individual’s daily functioning.","bbox":[91.0395,239.96536,396.74036,250.96536],"origin":[91.0395,248.46484],"font":"Helvetica","size":11.0,"colour":"#000000","direction":[1.0,0.0]},{"text":"- Moderate-to-Severe (20–24): Scores in this range indicate significant psychological distress,","bbox":[91.0395,252.06534,545.87842,263.06534],"origin":[91.0395,260.56482],"font":"Helvetica","size":11.0,"colour":"#000000","direction":[1.0,0.0]},{"text":"where symptoms are likely to interfere with daily functioning and require clinical attention.","bbox":[91.0395,264.16531,523.86743,275.16531],"origin":[91.0395,272.66479],"font":"Helvetica","size":11.0,"colour":"#000000","direction":[1.0,0.0]},{"text":"- Severe (25 and above): Scores in this range indicate severe distress, suggesting a high level","bbox":[91.0395,276.26529,548.9696,287.26529],"origin":[91.0395,284.76477],"font":"Helvetica","size":11.0,"colour":"#000000","direction":[1.0,0.0]},{"text":"of psychological impairment and an urgent need for clinical intervention. People who score in","bbox":[91.0395,288.36526,542.23755,299.36526],"origin":[91.0395,296.86475],"font":"Helvetica","size":11.0,"colour":"#000000","direction":[1.0,0.0]},{"text":"this range almost certainly meet the diagnostic criteria for an anxiety, mood, or other mental","bbox":[91.0395,300.46524,536.1106,311.46524],"origin":[91.0395,308.96472],"font":"Helvetica","size":11.0,"colour":"#000000","direction":[1.0,0.0]},{"text":"disorder.","bbox":[91.0395,312.56522,133.82948,323.56522],"origin":[91.0395,321.0647],"font":"Helvetica","size":11.0,"colour":"#000000","direction":[1.0,0.0]},{"text":"In addition to the raw score, two percentiles are presented. The Clinical Percentile compares","bbox":[91.0395,336.76523,540.38953,347.76523],"origin":[91.0395,345.26471],"font":"Helvetica","size":11.0,"colour":"#000000","direction":[1.0,0.0]},{"text":"scores with young people presenting for mental health services. A percentile of 50 would","bbox":[91.0395,348.86523,521.45856,359.86523],"origin":[91.0395,357.36472],"font":"Helvetica","size":11.0,"colour":"#000000","direction":[1.0,0.0]},{"text":"indicate an average level of symptoms for a young person on first presentation to a service.","bbox":[91.0395,360.96524,534.91162,371.96524],"origin":[91.0395,369.46472],"font":"Helvetica","size":11.0,"colour":"#000000","direction":[1.0,0.0]},{"text":"NOTE: Please enter accurate date of birth in client profile as normative data differs by age (11 to","bbox":[91.0395,373.06525,559.98065,384.06525],"origin":[91.0395,381.56473],"font":"Helvetica","size":11.0,"colour":"#000000","direction":[1.0,0.0]},{"text":"13 year olds mean = 15.8, SD 7.12 while 14 to 16 year olds mean = 20.6, SD = 7.06).","bbox":[91.0395,385.16525,506.52057,396.16525],"origin":[91.0395,393.66473],"font":"Helvetica","size":11.0,"colour":"#000000","direction":[1.0,0.0]},{"text":"A Non-Clinical Percentile is also presented which compares scores against a group of healthy","bbox":[91.0395,409.36526,546.49457,420.36526],"origin":[91.0395,417.86475],"font":"Helvetica","size":11.0,"colour":"#000000","direction":[1.0,0.0]},{"text":"young people (M=6.1, SD=6.06). Most people presenting for services will likely score above the","bbox":[91.0395,421.46527,554.4585,432.46527],"origin":[91.0395,429.96475],"font":"Helvetica","size":11.0,"colour":"#000000","direction":[1.0,0.0]},{"text":"90th percentile compared to this normative sample.","bbox":[91.0395,433.56528,340.47543,444.56528],"origin":[91.0395,442.06476],"font":"Helvetica","size":11.0,"colour":"#000000","direction":[1.0,0.0]},{"text":"On first administration a plot is shown presenting the total raw score with the symptom severity","bbox":[91.0395,457.76529,550.76257,468.76529],"origin":[91.0395,466.26477],"font":"Helvetica","size":11.0,"colour":"#000000","direction":[1.0,0.0]},{"text":"levels in the background of the plot. If administered on multiple occasions, a plot is displayed","bbox":[91.0395,469.8653,541.02759,480.8653],"origin":[91.0395,478.36478],"font":"Helvetica","size":11.0,"colour":"#000000","direction":[1.0,0.0]},{"text":"showing the raw score over time to indicate change as a result of treatment.","bbox":[91.0395,481.9653,459.70453,492.9653],"origin":[91.0395,490.46478],"font":"Helvetica","size":11.0,"colour":"#000000","direction":[1.0,0.0]},{"text":"Client Responses","bbox":[34.3465,524.5257,151.8205,538.5257],"origin":[34.3465,535.33197],"font":"Helvetica-Bold","size":14.0,"colour":"#000000","direction":[1.0,0.0]},{"text":"Not 